          "notes": "About 40 GB of weights streamed through system RAM plus the 2.2 GB pi-H3 2-step adapter. Two steps (fixed: the adapter is trained for two), no CFG, pi-Flow scheduler, sigma shift 12/3. The last step outputs pixels, so the video VAE decoder is skipped. Same base files as the MiniMax H3 pack. Faster Attention (Sage) is supported; Sol-Attn and Spectrum are off on purpose. On a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti in the app: 5 s at 480p 31-33 s, 5 s at 768p 71 s, 15 s at 480p 97 s. A 15-second shot at the 768p tier does not fit in 12 GB (it ran out of system memory and stalled)."
